+### Usage accumulation
+
+The helper `accumulateUsage(accumulated, next)` combines a running token total with a single round's reported usage:
+
+- When neither the running total nor the incoming round carries usage, the result is `undefined`, so the hook receives nothing rather than a zero or `NaN` ([validated by: returns undefined when both sides have no usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L31)).
+- When the running total is `undefined` but the incoming round has usage, that round's value becomes the total ([validated by: returns incoming usage when the running total is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L35)).
+- When the running total has usage but the incoming round has none, the total is unchanged: a round that reported nothing contributes nothing ([validated by: returns the running total when incoming usage is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L39)).
+- When both sides carry usage, every token count is summed so the total reflects every provider call so far ([validated by: sums token counts when both sides have usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L43)).
+
 The frontend shows a spinner on the last tool entry while the stream is still processing (`isProcessing` is `true`). The `stream_end` message clears the processing state, which hides the spinner. This works correctly even when tool suppression prevents assistant entries from reaching the frontend. See [tool-responses.md](../hal-engine-tool-responses/spec.md) for details on client messages and suppression.
 
